  TEMPLATE OVERRIDE (scripts/swift-templates/modelEnum.mustache)

  Identical to the upstream swift5 modelEnum.mustache (openapi-generator 7.23.0,
  pinned in openapitools.json) except that generated model types additionally
  declare `Sendable`.

  Every model is an immutable-by-construction value type of Sendable members, so
  the conformance is sound. Without it, `static let` model fixtures (MockData.swift,
  TestFixtures.swift) are rejected under the Swift 6 language mode as
  "not concurrency-safe because non-'Sendable' type ... may have shared mutable state".
  The upstream swift6 generator emits Sendable models for the same reason; we stay on
  swift5 because swift6 also emits 14 API entry-point classes this project does not use.

  On a generator upgrade, re-extract the upstream template and re-apply the
  `, Sendable` additions. See
  docs/archive/completed-plans/ios-swift6-generated-networking-plan.md.
}}
